        {
          "id": 528768239,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Without this patch, only pcapng files are written.\nWith this patch applied, it will only work for pcap and pcapng files, which have the \"upper PDU\" encapsulation type. With other types, the following error message is produced for other sorts of files, even files that normally wireshark can convert pcapng files to:\n```\n$ ./run/tshark -F nettl -U \"OSI layer 4\" -r input.pcapng -w export.pcap\ntshark: The capture file being read can't be written as a \"nettl\" file.\n$ ./run/tshark -F snoop -U \"OSI layer 4\" -r input.pcapng -w export.pcap\ntshark: The capture file being read can't be written as a \"snoop\" file.\n```\n\nLong term, I do intend to make it possible to use an \"Export PDU\" tap to write out, e.g., selected Ethernet packets tunneled in some other protocol using any particular file format's regular encapsulation, but that requires other changes. For example, one need to check the encapsulation type in `export_pdu_packet()` in [tap_export_pdu.c](ui/tap_export_pdu.c) and then not writing the TLV structure if the encap type to be written is not `WTAP_ENCAP_WIRESHARK_UPPER_PDU` I think it would be useful to use certain Export PDU taps that take off lower layers without adding the special TLV structure, for feeding into other programs. One disadvantage of the TLV structure is that it is a variable number of bytes, so it can be harder to remove cleanly.\n\nHowever, that's not the intent or effect of this particular merge request, which only allows pcap in addition to the already allowed pcapng.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-03-13T23:34:03.230Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-03-13T23:34:03.230Z",
