        {
          "id": 528768450,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "For this patch, it still always uses `WTAP_ENCAP_WIRESHARK_UPPER_PDU` which results in a `WTAP_ERR_UNWRITABLE_ENCAP` error for any thing other than pcap and pcapng, as you say. But it does mean that `./run/tshark -F nsecpcap -U \"OSI layer 4\" -r input.pcap -w export.pcap` writes a nanosecond pcap file (with the appropriate encapsulation type) instead of (perhaps surprisingly) writing a pcapng file.",
          "author": {
