        {
          "id": 528770059,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It's necessary to change ui/tap_export_pdu.c, because the existing code incorrectly calls  `wtap_wtap_encap_to_pcap_encap()` on `WTAP_ENCAP_WIRESHARK_UPPER_PDU` before setting `rec.rec_header.packet_header.pkt_encap` to the value. But `rec.rec_header.packet_header.pkt_encap` is supposed to have wiretap encap values, not pcap encap values. `wtap_wtap_encap_to_pcap_encap()` gets called later by the various file format specific dump functions, as it has to be. Since that function gets called twice, it ends up returning incorrect values, which ends up resulting in the encapsulation types being wrong and the file encapsulation being changed to `WTAP_ENCAP_PER_PACKET`, which pcap doesn't support (only pcapng).\n\nSo without changing ui/tap_export_pdu.c to remove that erroneous function call, it won't actually write to pcap files, just pcapng. It will create an empty pcap file, just header, after erroring out with `WTAP_ERR_ENCAP_PER_PACKET_UNSUPPORTED`",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
